    "240.4(B) permits the next higher standard rating when the conductor ampacity lies between standard ratings, the selected device does not exceed 800 A, and the conductors are not part of a branch circuit supplying more than one receptacle for portable cord-and-plug loads. The load must still fit the conductor. This permission does not override a 240.4(D) small-conductor limit.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "240.4(B) permits the next higher standard rating when the conductor ampacity lies between standard ratings, the selected device does not exceed 800 A, and the conductors are not part of a branch circuit supplying more than one receptacle for portable cord-and-plug loads. The load must still fit the conductor. This permission does not override a 240.4(D) small-conductor limit."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "240.4(D) caps this size at %lld A regardless of the table. That cap is the number to protect at, not %lld A.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "240.4(D) caps this size at %lld A regardless of the table. That cap is the number to protect at, not %lld A."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "240.4(D) then caps 12 AWG copper at 20 A no matter what the table says.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "240.4(D) then caps 12 AWG copper at 20 A no matter what the table says."
