    "28 × 1.25 = 35 A. The 125% is the continuous-load treatment motors always get. 32.2 A would be 115%, which belongs to overload sizing and not to conductors.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "28 × 1.25 = 35 A. The 125% is the continuous-load treatment motors always get. 32.2 A would be 115%, which belongs to overload sizing and not to conductors."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "3 VA per square foot, the 3000 VA and 35% bands, the range and dryer tables, and the 75% appliance factor. Article 220 was renumbered for the 2023 cycle; the values did not change, and both section numbers are cited.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
