          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A rod, pipe or plate electrode has a ceiling: the conductor running to it is never required to exceed 6 AWG copper, because the electrode itself cannot carry more than that. A concrete-encased electrode caps at 4 AWG. A ground ring caps at the size of the ring.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
