    "Estimate voltage drop on a 120 V single-phase circuit carrying 16 A on 10 AWG copper for 100 feet one way. Use the resistive formula with K = 12.9 ohm-cmil/ft, neglecting reactance and power-factor effects. Round to 0.1 V.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Estimate voltage drop on a 120 V single-phase circuit carrying 16 A on 10 AWG copper for 100 feet one way. Use the resistive formula with K = 12.9 ohm-cmil/ft, neglecting reactance and power-factor effects. Round to 0.1 V."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Estimate voltage drop using K = 12.9 for copper or 21.2 for aluminum in ohm-cmil/ft. Use the resistive formula, neglect reactance and power-factor effects, and round to 0.1 V.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
