        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every calculation you work here is one you'll work faster on the exam."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every number in this app comes from the %@, and every table it computes from is unchanged across the %@. Electrician is a study aid, not a code book. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the NFPA. It teaches concepts and calculations in original wording and cites article numbers so you can verify each one yourself. Your jurisdiction may examine against a different edition or amend it locally, so always check the code in force where you work.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every number in this app comes from the %@, and every table it computes from is unchanged across the %@. Electrician is a study aid, not a code book. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the NFPA. It teaches concepts and calculations in original wording and cites article numbers so you can verify each one yourself. Your jurisdiction may examine against a different edition or amend it locally, so always check the code in force where you work."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every one of the four conditions has to hold. This is the row that lets a homeowner's yard light go in at a foot, and it is the row candidates quote for a 240 volt circuit or a 30 ampere one, where it does not apply. Miss any condition and the run goes back to its own column.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every one of the four conditions has to hold. This is the row that lets a homeowner's yard light go in at a foot, and it is the row candidates quote for a 240 volt circuit or a 30 ampere one, where it does not apply. Miss any condition and the run goes back to its own column."
          }
        }
      }
    },
