    "That is an overload calculation, not short-circuit protection. The two are separate devices with separate rules: overload runs at 115% or 125% of the NAMEPLATE, while the branch-circuit device runs at the Table 430.52 percentage of the TABLE current.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "That is an overload calculation, not short-circuit protection. The two are separate devices with separate rules: overload runs at 115% or 125% of the NAMEPLATE, while the branch-circuit device runs at the Table 430.52 percentage of the TABLE current."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That is an overload calculation, not short-circuit protection. The two are separate devices with separate rules: overload runs at 115% or 125% of the NAMEPLATE, while the branch-circuit device runs at the Table 430.52(C)(1) percentage of the TABLE current.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
