    "The 12-inch burial row: what has to be true to use it?": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 12-inch burial row: what has to be true to use it?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 125% applies in two separate places: 210.19(A) for the conductor and 210.20(A) for the device. Applying it to only one gives you a conductor its own breaker will not protect, or a breaker that nuisance-trips.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 125% applies in two separate places: 210.19(A) for the conductor and 210.20(A) for the device. Applying it to only one gives you a conductor its own breaker will not protect, or a breaker that nuisance-trips."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 75°C column gives 12 AWG copper as 25 A.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 75°C column gives 12 AWG copper as 25 A."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 75°C column shows 20 A and the 90°C column shows 25 A, and both are irrelevant here. 240.4(D) caps 14 AWG copper at 15 A. If you answered 20 or 25 you read the table and stopped one rule short.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 75°C column shows 20 A and the 90°C column shows 25 A, and both are irrelevant here. 240.4(D) caps 14 AWG copper at 15 A. If you answered 20 or 25 you read the table and stopped one rule short."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 75°C termination allows 65 A, which is higher, so the derated 52.2 A is the limit.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 75°C termination allows 65 A, which is higher, so the derated 52.2 A is the limit."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 75°C termination limits it to %lld A, and the lower number wins, so the answer is %@ A.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 75°C termination limits it to %lld A, and the lower number wins, so the answer is %@ A."
          }
        }
      }
    },
