      }
    },
    "The technical paper overlaps the master exam. The business-and-law paper is separate and this app does not cover it.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The technical paper overlaps the master exam. The business-and-law paper is separate and this app does not cover it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The termination is the weak point, so it sets the ceiling. You may derate from the 90°C value, but the final answer can never exceed the 75°C ampacity of that conductor.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The termination is the weak point, so it sets the ceiling. You may derate from the 90°C value, but the final answer can never exceed the 75°C ampacity of that conductor."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The thirty inches does not have to be centred on the equipment, and it may overlap the working space of adjacent equipment. What it may not do is be blocked by a door: the space has to allow any equipment door or hinged panel to open at least ninety degrees. A panel in a closet that only opens sixty degrees fails on the door, not on the thirty inches.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The thirty inches does not have to be centred on the equipment, and it may overlap the working space of adjacent equipment. What it may not do is be blocked by a door: the space has to allow any equipment door or hinged panel to open at least ninety degrees. A panel in a closet that only opens sixty degrees fails on the door, not on the thirty inches."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The three temperature columns for copper and aluminum. The table this app derates from, and the one an exam question hands you a conductor and asks about.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The three temperature columns for copper and aluminum. The table this app derates from, and the one an exam question hands you a conductor and asks about."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The twelve inches is measured to the cable entry and assumes the box has a clamp. A single-gang nonmetallic box without a clamp gets its own allowance: the cable is secured within eight inches of the box instead, measured along the sheath, with a length of sheath inside the box.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The twelve inches is measured to the cable entry and assumes the box has a clamp. A single-gang nonmetallic box without a clamp gets its own allowance: the cable is secured within eight inches of the box instead, measured along the sheath, with a length of sheath inside the box."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The two articles that decide a pass": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The two articles that decide a pass"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The unrounded minimum is %@ A after correction and adjustment. The option is reported to the nearest 0.1 A; select actual conductors using the unrounded minimum and Table 310.16.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The unrounded minimum is %@ A after correction and adjustment. The option is reported to the nearest 0.1 A; select actual conductors using the unrounded minimum and Table 310.16."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The usual clear height is 6.5 feet or the equipment height if greater. Existing dwelling installations at 200 A or less have a specific exception. Dedicated space above the equipment is a separate rule; do not treat the whole room above the working space as that dedicated column.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The usual clear height is 6.5 feet or the equipment height if greater. Existing dwelling installations at 200 A or less have a specific exception. Dedicated space above the equipment is a separate rule; do not treat the whole room above the working space as that dedicated column."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The width is thirty inches or the width of the equipment, whichever is greater, so equipment wider than thirty inches sets its own working space. The thirty inches is a floor, not the answer.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The width is thirty inches or the width of the equipment, whichever is greater, so equipment wider than thirty inches sets its own working space. The thirty inches is a floor, not the answer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
