    "They are covered by the 3 VA per square foot": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "They are covered by the 3 VA per square foot"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "They go into the subtotal that the demand table then discounts, alongside the general lighting and the laundry circuit. Adding the two 1500 VA circuits afterward instead of in the 35% band inflates the calculated load by 1950 VA, which is enough to move the answer up a standard size on a small house.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "They go into the subtotal that the demand table then discounts, alongside the general lighting and the laundry circuit. Adding the two 1500 VA circuits afterward instead of in the 35% band inflates the calculated load by 1950 VA, which is enough to move the answer up a standard size on a small house."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "They go into the subtotal that the demand table then discounts, alongside the general lighting and the laundry circuit. Adding them afterward at 100% inflates the service by roughly 2900 VA, which is enough to move the answer up a standard size on a small house.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "They go into the subtotal that the demand table then discounts, alongside the general lighting and the laundry circuit. Adding them afterward at 100% inflates the service by roughly 2900 VA, which is enough to move the answer up a standard size on a small house."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "They multiply. A 0.87 correction and a 0.80 adjustment give 0.696 of the starting value, not 0.80 and not a 33% reduction. Taking only the worse of the two is a common shortcut and it produces an unsafe answer.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "They multiply. A 0.87 correction and a 0.80 adjustment give 0.696 of the starting value, not 0.80 and not a 33% reduction. Taking only the worse of the two is a common shortcut and it produces an unsafe answer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
