        }
      }
    },
    "You carried the fastened-in-place appliances at 100%. Four or more of them on the same service come in at 75% under 220.53, and the range, dryer, heating and air conditioning are not part of that count.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You carried the fastened-in-place appliances at 100%. Four or more of them on the same service come in at 75% under 220.53, and the range, dryer, heating and air conditioning are not part of that count."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You carried the general lighting at 100%. Only the first 3000 VA stays whole; the rest of it up to 120,000 VA comes in at 35%. That demand factor is most of the difference between a 200 A service and a 400 A one.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You carried the general lighting at 100%. Only the first 3000 VA stays whole; the rest of it up to 120,000 VA comes in at 35%. That demand factor is most of the difference between a 200 A service and a 400 A one."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You counted each equipment ground separately. All the grounds in a box together are ONE allowance, however many there are.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You counted each equipment ground separately. All the grounds in a box together are ONE allowance, however many there are."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You counted each equipment ground separately. Up to four entering equipment grounds use one allowance. Each additional entering ground or bonding jumper adds a quarter allowance. Internal pigtails do not count.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You counted each equipment ground separately. Up to four entering equipment grounds use one allowance. Each additional entering ground or bonding jumper adds a quarter allowance. Internal pigtails do not count."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You counted each yoke as one allowance. A device yoke counts as TWO.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You counted each yoke as one allowance. A device yoke counts as TWO."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You derated correctly and then stopped. The result still has to be capped at the termination column, which is usually 75°C.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You derated correctly and then stopped. The result still has to be capped at the termination column, which is usually 75°C."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You derated from the 75°C column. Corrections and adjustments start in the conductor's own insulation column, and 75°C only comes back at the end as the termination cap.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You derated from the 75°C column. Corrections and adjustments start in the conductor's own insulation column, and 75°C only comes back at the end as the termination cap."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You dropped to the row below. Table 250.122 is a set of not-exceeding bands: a rating between two rows reads the row ABOVE it, so a 45 A device takes the 60 A row.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You dropped to the row below. Table 250.122 is a set of not-exceeding bands: a rating between two rows reads the row ABOVE it, so a 45 A device takes the 60 A row."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You have no mistakes waiting. Answer a few questions and anything you miss will show up here.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
