    "You protected at the ampacity table value and missed 240.4(D). For 14, 12 and 10 AWG the small-conductor ceiling overrides the table.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You protected at the ampacity table value and missed 240.4(D). For 14, 12 and 10 AWG the small-conductor ceiling overrides the table."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You read the copper service bands for an aluminum service, or the reverse. Table 250.66 has a separate set of bands for each service metal, and they do not line up.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You read the copper service bands for an aluminum service, or the reverse. Table 250.66 has a separate set of bands for each service metal, and they do not line up."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You read the other metal's column. Aluminum needs more area than copper for the same job, so the two columns are never the same size on a row.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You read the other metal's column. Aluminum needs more area than copper for the same job, so the two columns are never the same size on a row."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You read the table on one conductor of the parallel set. The table is entered on the EQUIVALENT area of the whole set: two 250 kcmil in parallel is read as 500 kcmil.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You read the table on one conductor of the parallel set. The table is entered on the EQUIVALENT area of the whole set: two 250 kcmil in parallel is read as 500 kcmil."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You read the wrong voltage column. The same horsepower draws roughly half the current at twice the voltage, so picking the wrong column is a 2x error, not a rounding one.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You read the wrong voltage column. The same horsepower draws roughly half the current at twice the voltage, so picking the wrong column is a 2x error, not a rounding one."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You rounded down to the next standard rating. Motor branch-circuit protection is the exception: 430.52(C)(1) Exception 1 lets you go UP to the next standard size when the percentage does not land on one, because the device has to survive starting current.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You rounded down to the next standard rating. Motor branch-circuit protection is the exception: 430.52(C)(1) Exception 1 lets you go UP to the next standard size when the percentage does not land on one, because the device has to survive starting current."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "You rounded up to the next standard rating. Without a next-size-up allowance the protection goes to the largest standard rating at or BELOW the conductor's usable ampacity.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You rounded up to the next standard rating. Without a next-size-up allowance the protection goes to the largest standard rating at or BELOW the conductor's usable ampacity."
          }
        }
      }
    },
